        "code": {
          "text": "Epigastric pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Intermittent for several months; burning and gnawing, worse when the stomach is empty and often late at night a few hours after meals; relieved by food and over-the-counter antacids. Over the last two weeks, pain has occurred most nights and wakes the patient 3–4 times per week."
